  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "y[n] = sum over k of x[n-k] * h[k]",
        "No output is fed back, thus the filter is stable whatever the coefficients",
        "Every frequency is held back by the same time, which is half the length"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How the library gets there",
      "items": [
        "The ideal filter is a sinc in time, and a sinc runs for ever",
        "A window cuts it to a length that can be held; the window sets the stop band",
        "The length sets how sharp the edge between pass and stop can be"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What it costs you",
      "items": [
        "The cost is that length: dozens of coefficients where a biquad needs five",
        "Use iir when the operations for each sample matter more than the shape",
        "Use this when the shape of the signal must stay as it is"
      ]
